    "https://external-careers.jobs.unsw.edu.au/en/job/539215/casual-academic-talent-pool-business-centre-for-social-impact-csi": {
      "title": "Casual Academic Talent Pool - Business - Centre for Social Impact (CSI)",
      "description": "Casual Academic Talent Pool - Business - Centre for Social Impact (CSI) Apply now Job no: 539215 Work type: Casual Location: Sydney, NSW Categories: Tutor, Senior Lecturer, Professor, Lecturer Casual Roles in 2026, Centre for Social Impact Make a difference to people’s lives Play a key part at UNSW Business School Multiple Positions Available The Centre for Social Impact is seeking applications for casual opportunities in 2025 courses. The positions are only available to those who are eligible to work in Australia, those who have postgraduate qualifications and who are able to demonstrate understanding of the content for the courses they wish to work in, and those who hold a qualification at least one level higher than that held by the students enrolled in the course/qualification in which they are teaching. We expect to offer both on-campus and online activities in 2025 and that in addition to tutor-type roles (both on-campus and those involving virtual tutorial delivery), there will also be some opportunities in online support (e.g., monitoring Moodle forums), as well as marking (online or otherwise), and in some cases online consultation and the production of online resources. Please revert to the Position Description below for more details. The application will include screening questions so we can better assess your suitability and potentially meet your need for flexibility. UNSW is committed to equity diversity and inclusion. Applications from women, people of culturally and linguistically diverse backgrounds, those living with disabilities, members of the LGBTIQ+ community; and people of Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander descent, are encouraged. UNSW provides workplace adjustments for people with disability, and access to flexible work options for eligible staff. The University reserves the right not to proceed with any appointment. Closing Dates: Applications will be reviewed on a rolling basis. Pre-Employment Checks Aligned with UN