    "https://external-careers.jobs.unsw.edu.au/en/job/539077/casual-academic-talent-pool-ada-social-sciences": {
      "title": "Casual Academic Talent Pool - ADA - Social Sciences",
      "description": "Casual Academic Talent Pool - ADA - Social Sciences Apply now Job no: 539077 Work type: Casual Location: Sydney, NSW Categories: Tutor, Lecturer, Other, Demonstrator The School of Social Sciences in the Faculty of Arts, Design and Architecture is seeking expressions of interest from qualified individuals for casual teaching opportunities, in the areas of Global Development, Politics and International Relations, Sociology & Anthropology, Social Science & Policy and Social Work. About the role As a casual tutor, your role is to lead teaching in tutorials and provide support to the Course Convenor. Your duties as a tutor include: Familiarity with the course content Preparations for tutorial classes each week, including weekly readings, materials and creating teaching slides Marking duties If your EOI is accepted, the School of Social Sciences will be in contact with you to provide further information about the particular role. Additional Information The School of Social Sciences will consider your application if your skills, qualifications, and experience are suitable. If there is no suitable opportunity immediately available, your EOI will be retained for consideration in subsequent teaching terms. The EOI portal will allow you to submit your CV, to outline your qualifications and experience, and to nominate which disciplines/courses you would like to teach. Please note that you must have working rights in Australia and have an Australian bank account. Overseas applications cannot be considered. UNSW is committed to equity diversity and inclusion. Applications from women, people of culturally and linguistically diverse backgrounds, those living with disabilities, members of the LGBTIQ+ community; and people of Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander descent, are encouraged. UNSW provides workplace adjustments for people with disability, and access to flexible work options for eligible staff. The University reserves the right not to proceed with any appointment. Pre-Employment Checks Aligned with UNSW’s focus on cultivating a workplace defined by safety, ethical conduct, and strong integrity preferred candidates will be required to participate in a combination of pre-employment checks relevant to the role they have applied for. These pre-employment checks may include a combination of some of the following checks: National and International Criminal history checks Entitlement to work and ID checks Working With Children Checks Completion of a Gender-Based Violence Prevention Declaration Verification of relevant qualifications Verification of relevant professional membership Employment history and reference checks Financial responsibility assessments/checks. Medical Checks and Assessments Compliance with the necessary combination of these checks is a condition of employment at UNSW. #LI-DNI Position Description Advertised: 01 Apr 2026 AUS Eastern Daylight Time Applications close: Back to search results Apply now Refer a friend Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App"
    },
    "https://external-careers.jobs.unsw.edu.au/en/job/539085/casual-academic-talent-pool-school-of-population-health-medicine": {
      "title": "Casual Academic Talent Pool - School of Population Health - Medicine",
      "description": "Casual Academic Talent Pool - School of Population Health - Medicine Apply now Job no: 539085 Work type: Casual Location: Sydney, NSW Categories: Tutor, Lecturer, Other, Demonstrator The School of Population Health is internationally recognised as a leader in Public Health and Health Leadership and Management with particular research strengths in Epidemiology and Infectious Diseases, Health Services Management, Global Health, Indigenous Health and Primary Health Care.  The School has a core focus to investigate and provide new knowledge to help inform policy, governance, organisation, work and leadership in the health sector through cross disciplinary research with both academia and industry. The School of Population Health is seeking applications for casual opportunities. Join the SPH team to : Make a difference to people’s lives Play a key part at UNSW SPH Multiple Positions Available The positions are available to those who have studied and have practical experience in the development and/or delivery of teaching in public health, health leadership and management, global health and medicine . Casual academic staff will work closely with the course convenors and will be expected to demonstrate understanding of the content for the courses they wish to work in. There are opportunities to contribute to both on-campus and online activities and the following roles are available: Tutoring and or Facilitations online support (e.g., monitoring Moodle forums, online moderation), marking online consultation and the production of online resources. Familiarity with Moodle is essential Additional Information We encourage Expressions of Interest from experienced tutors, demonstrators, markers and lecturers who are excited to collaborate across different disciplines and be a part of an integrated teaching team. We are recruiting tutors and markers throughout 2026 and you will be contacted for an interview if your skills, qualifications, and experience are suitable. The EOI portal will allow you to select which courses you would like to contribute to and the extent of your qualifications and experience so we can better assess your suitability and potentially meet your need for flexibility. Please note that you must have working rights in Australia and have an Australian bank account. Overseas applications cannot be considered. UNSW is committed to equity diversity and inclusion. Applications from women, people of culturally and linguistically diverse backgrounds, those living with disabilities, members of the LGBTIQ+ community; and people of Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander descent, are encouraged. UNSW provides workplace adjustments for people with disability, and access to flexible work options for eligible staff. The University reserves the right not to proceed with any appointment. Closing Dates: To apply, please complete the linked application form. Note that casual appointments will be made on a term-by-term basis, and that term dates are approximately as follows: Term 1 (mid-Feb - mid-May) Term 2 (late May - late Aug) Term 3 (mid-Sept - mid-Dec) Summer Term (Jan - early Feb) Pre-Employment Checks Aligned with UNSW’s focus on cultivating a workplace defined by safety, ethical conduct, and strong integrity preferred candidates will be required to participate in a combination of pre-employment checks relevant to the role they have applied for. These pre-employment checks may include a combination of some of the following checks: National and International Criminal history checks Entitlement to work and ID checks Working With Children Checks Completion of a Gender-Based Violence Prevention Declaration Verification of relevant qualifications Verification of relevant professional membership Employment history and reference checks Financial responsibility assessments/checks. Medical Checks and Assessments Compliance with the necessary combination of these checks is a condition of employment at UNSW. #LI-DNI Position Description Advertised: 01 Apr 2026 AUS Eastern Daylight Time Applications close: Back to search results Apply now Refer a friend Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App"
    },
